    web_documents {
      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFLl9Ydy9CTBn0DS6Y63JZg0M4SkhwO4J-gIQnUGZixoqa2KCZRXGu4uHE9Z0SK93UYbfhYgJ18vplwJNfREPT-YqaYVBu8Pq4weGB_I9HXkxbnbzMmpJ-osDViuEN4WaXQi18AiNqvgC4PWjXs-nMCSrXllcH5JcaE_bzlgNZL"
      title: "github.com"
    }
    web_documents {
      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGQYw5I25GsoUtWF7nL_AfvmHCJVcbKORDDL2X_8dNNUnfod_4nqrmGSLsjeVjzYGQLF4UQDELa_ihwubHKeuJpGlNPQRqEpIfrMEyDAXziJS3hViEsyYvfxLMhEvwDtwEiivraxmattXRrOkf94wzJInWZ"
      title: "github.com"
    }
    summary: "The `yahoo-finance2` library, an unofficial API for Yahoo Finance, incorporates robust validation and error logging mechanisms to ensure data integrity and assist developers in handling unexpected responses. By default, the library validates all results received from Yahoo to prevent unexpected crashes and ensure that your code receives the expected input[1][2].\n\nHere\'s a breakdown of how validation and error logging are managed:\n\n**Validation**\n*   **Purpose:** Validation is crucial for safeguarding your application from unpredictable data. If `yahoo-finance2` receives data that doesn\'t conform to its internal schema, it will throw a `FailedYahooValidationError`[1][3][2]. This can occur due to various reasons, such as network issues, HTTP errors, missing resources, or even delisted stocks[1].\n*   **`FailedYahooValidationError`**: When this error occurs, the library often provides a `result` object that is partially validated or coerced, allowing developers to extract usable data even when full validation fails[1][3][2]. Additionally, the `error.errors` property provides an array of specific schema validation errors for more detailed inspection[2].\n*   **Skipping Validation:** For situations where strict schema validation is not desired or when dealing with known inconsistencies in Yahoo\'s responses, you can bypass runtime schema validation by setting `validateResult: false` within the `moduleOpts` argument of your API call. This will prevent validation errors from being thrown[1][2].\n*   **Schema Adjustments:** Community discussions and workarounds suggest that when Yahoo Finance data doesn\'t perfectly align with the expected schema, adjusting the schema to make certain fields optional or providing default values can help prevent validation failures[3].\n*   **\"Additional Properties\":** Since version 2.2 (March 2022), `yahoo-finance2` allows for \"additional properties\" in the results. This means that if Yahoo introduces new fields, the library will not throw an error, thus preventing existing deployments from breaking[2].\n\n**Error Logging**\n*   **Disabling Validation Log Errors:** By default, `yahoo-finance2` provides verbose error logging on validation failures to assist in debugging[2]. However, you can disable this logging by initializing the `YahooFinance` instance with `logErrors: false` within the `validation` configuration object. For example: `const yahooFinance = new YahooFinance({ validation: { logErrors: false } });`[2].\n*   **General Error Handling:** The library recommends wrapping API calls in `try...catch` blocks to inspect errors and determine appropriate handling. Errors can include `HTTPError` (where the message property will be the HTTP response status text) or generic `Error` objects for unhandled cases[1].\n\nSources:\n[1] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGZELw30PGumud0NRCOeWG4xfkiTX4EHvHt5P0LysPGE8IfU8z9bEI2taCoJQoctHFGHyeTaIORkIFgzT0zBOQsqiJZttCVLx-3ik6hAAAZyY-qE1bE-DabwZWnxwRcA5Y_ROB9DETJ9mUrqYvp4VaB0OhufTNvS0EDwg4=)\n[2] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFLl9Ydy9CTBn0DS6Y63JZg0M4SkhwO4J-gIQnUGZixoqa2KCZRXGu4uHE9Z0SK93UYbfhYgJ18vplwJNfREPT-YqaYVBu8Pq4weGB_I9HXkxbnbzMmpJ-osDViuEN4WaXQi18AiNqvgC4PWjXs-nMCSrXllcH5JcaE_bzlgNZL)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGQYw5I25GsoUtWF7nL_AfvmHCJVcbKORDDL2X_8dNNUnfod_4nqrmGSLsjeVjzYGQLF4UQDELa_ihwubHKeuJpGlNPQRqEpIfrMEyDAXziJS3hViEsyYvfxLMhEvwDtwEiivraxmattXRrOkf94wzJInWZ)"
    search_type: SEARCH_WEB_TYPE_WEB
  }
