ting its behavior in both development and production. In ES module mode, the class constructor is returned directly, with `YahooFinance.default` being undefined, so the class itself is returned. In CommonJS environments, we get a module object, and the `.default` property correctly provides the desired class constructor. This handles all cases and feels complete!\n\n\n"
