    thinking: "**Analyzing Sync Status**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently focused on the `/src/App.tsx` file and the `syncStatus` component. It seems this handles those on-screen notifications and overlays related to synchronization, right? I\'m examining how it integrates within the Home view, particularly the database connection status banner. I\'m trying to get a better sense of how it\'s used and where it fits within the broader UI.\n\n\n**Examining User State**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user authentication flow within the sync status area. Specifically, I\'m looking at how the UI reacts depending on whether a user is logged in (cloud backup active) or in local storage mode (offline-first). I\'m tracing how the \"Backup em Nuvem Ativo\" or \"Modo de Armazenamento Local (Offline-first)\" text is displayed. The code related to the user\'s login and logout buttons is also of interest here.\n\n\n**Investigating Connection Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"Conectar com Google\" button and related user state handling. I\'m scrutinizing the `isLoggingIn` state, and how the text dynamically changes based on login status. I\'m focusing on the user\'s email display, cloud backup messaging, and conditional display of the sync status overlay. The connection state logic and user data messaging are key.\n\n\n**Scrutinizing Sync Status Display**\n\nI\'m now examining the visual feedback for sync status, focusing on the conditional rendering of the status overlay. Specifically, I\'m analyzing the styling applied to the border, background color, and text color, based on states like \'syncing,\' \'success,\' or \'error.\' Also, the animation and content of each sync status alert are being scrutinized.\n\n\n**Analyzing Backup Flow**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the backup and restore buttons, which are only visible when a user is authenticated. I\'m scrutinizing the `handleSyncToDrive` and `handleSyncFromDrive` functions. The styling and visual cues for these are also key here. I\'m investigating how the buttons\' states (enabled/disabled, text, etc.) change based on the user\'s state and data availability.\n\n\n**Refining UI Element Placement**\n\nI\'m now considering the removal of the cloud backup/sync-related elements from the Home view and repositioning them exclusively within the settings interface. The refresh quotes button in the home screen is an additional area of concern and must remain available on the home screen. I\'m focusing on ensuring these changes maintain a clear and intuitive user experience.\n\n\n**Refining Quote Refresh**\n\nI\'m now refining the quote refresh functionality. I\'m focusing on the \"Atualizar Cota\303\247\303\265es\" button placement, considering options like a subtle floating refresh button, a top bar button, or keeping the header clean. I\'m leaning toward incorporating it into the desktop header or as a small button in the Home view, prioritizing a clean design. I\'m revisiting the Header.tsx implementation to finalize the best integration.\n\n\n**Evaluating Placement Options**\n\nI\'m now exploring the optimal placement for sync status messaging, potentially relocating it to the Settings panel. I\'m focusing on incorporating a dedicated status message area within the \"Google Drive Integration\" section, mirroring the functionality of the previous banner. I\'m reviewing the existing settings tab structure for seamless integration.\n\n\n**Evaluating Backup Functionality**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user authentication elements within the settings interface, scrutinizing the \"Salvar Backup Now\" and \"Carregar Backup\" buttons. I\'m focusing on the user email display, their respective click handlers and state management to ensure a clear user experience and data flow for backups.\n\n\n**Analyzing Login Interface**\n\nI\'m now examining the login interface within settings, specifically the \"Restaurar do Drive\" and \"Desconectar Conta Google\" buttons. The `handleLogin` and `handleLogout` functions are a k